-- =====================================================================
-- Session 146 — Matt 16 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 16''s extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2), S132 (Matt 3), S133 (Matt 4),
-- S134 (Matt 5), S135 (Matt 6), S137 (Matt 7-8 paired), S138 (Matt 9),
-- S139 (Matt 10), S140 (Matt 11), S142 (Matt 12), S143 (Matt 13), S144
-- (Matt 14), and S145 (Matt 15) extras-tier coverage. Single chapter
-- migration — Matt 16 is the Caesarea-Philippi-confession chapter, with
-- the chapter''s framework-major moments landing in (a) the Pharisaic-
-- and-Sadducean confederation''s-sign-from-heaven demand and the King''s
-- refusal with the sign-of-Yonah (Jonah) restated (vv.1-4); (b) the
-- leaven-of-the-Pharisees-and-Sadducees-named-explicitly-as-their-
-- doctrine (vv.5-12); (c) the Caesarea-Philippi confession at Kefa''s
-- (Peter''s) *thou art the Messiah, the Son of the living Elohim (God)*
-- with the King''s-response *upon this rock I will build my assembly ...
-- and I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* and the
-- gates-of-hell-shall-not-prevail substance (vv.13-20 — the short.md
-- walks the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 22:15-25 Shevna-and-Elyakim succession
-- as the prophetic-architecture for the demotion-of-the-self-creden-
-- tialing-Shevna-class (the contemporary Pharisaic-and-Sadducean
-- second-Temple-aristocracy) and the elevation-of-the-Elyakim-class-
-- of-apostolic-stewardship the King establishes at Kefa''s confession);
-- (d) the first-explicit-passion-prediction at the *must* (*dei*) of
-- the divine-necessity drawn from Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 53''s suffering-
-- servant and Zekharyah (Zechariah) 13:7''s smitten-shepherd, with
-- Kefa''s (Peter''s) rebuke and the King''s *get thee behind me, Satan*
-- counter-rebuke echoing the Matt 4 wilderness-temptation-responses
-- (vv.21-23); (e) the take-up-the-cross discipleship-cost teaching
-- with the reward-according-to-works post-harvest-sifting substance
-- and the *some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till
-- they see the Son of Adam coming in his kingdom* bridge into the
-- transfiguration (vv.24-28).
--
-- Matt 16 reading-target: the chapter walks five narrative-movements
-- with the Tanakh-substance carrying the heaviest framework-bearing
-- anchors directly (Tehillim (Psalm) 2:1-2 for the Pharisaic-and-
-- Sadducean confederation against the King; Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 22:15-25
-- for the Shevna-and-Elyakim Davidic-stewardship-keys succession; Deva-
-- rim (Deuteronomy) 32:4, Tehillim (Psalm) 18:2, Yeshayahu (Isaiah)
-- 28:16, Tehillim (Psalm) 118:22 for the Rock-substance and the
-- chief-corner-stone-and-foundation-stone the King is; Yeshayahu
-- (Isaiah) 38:10, Tehillim (Psalm) 9:13, Iyov (Job) 38:17 for the
-- gates-of-Sheol substance the gates-of-Hades translates; Yeshayahu
-- (Isaiah) 53:1-12, Zekharyah (Zechariah) 13:7, Zekharyah (Zechariah)
-- 12:10 for the suffering-servant-smitten-shepherd-pierced-one Tanakh-
-- substance the first-passion-prediction draws-from; Tehillim (Psalm)
-- 62:12 + Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 17:10 for the reward-according-to-works
-- substance). The extras-library adds five framework-bearing thread-
-- clusters: 1 Enoch 46:2-3 + 48:2-3 + Wisdom of Solomon 2:13, 18 on
-- the Son-of-Adam / Son-of-the-living-Elohim named-before-the-founda-
-- tion substance Kefa''s (Peter''s) confession at v.16 articulates
-- (Thread 1 — FRAMEWORK-MAJOR); 1 Enoch 49:2 + 51:3 + 62:7 + 69:27 on
-- the Elect-One / Son-of-Adam given the throne and the sum-of-judgment-
-- committed-unto-him substance the keys-of-the-kingdom at v.19 commit
-- to the apostolic-stewardship as the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 22:22 key-of-
-- the-house-of-David delegated-from-the-King-who-holds-the-master-key
-- (Thread 2 — FRAMEWORK-MAJOR); Wisdom of Solomon 2:12, 16, 20 + 3:1
-- + 5:1 on the righteous-one persecuted-and-condemned-with-a-shameful-
-- death and vindicated-in-the-resurrection substance the first-passion-
-- prediction at v.21 draws-from (Thread 3); Wisdom of Solomon 1:13 +
-- 16:13 + 1 Enoch 51:1 + 2 Esdras 4:35 on the gates-of-Sheol-and-the-
-- resurrection-substance the gates-of-hell-shall-not-prevail at v.18
-- articulates (Thread 4); Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16:12, 14 + 35:19 +
-- 2 Esdras 7:32, 35 on the reward-according-to-works post-harvest-
-- sifting substance the Son-of-Adam-coming-and-rewarding at v.27
-- articulates (Thread 5). Apocalypse of Abraham, Ascension of Isaiah,
-- Adam-Eve Conflict, Jubilees, Jasher, and Sonnini''s Acts of Paul do
-- not surface framework-bearing Matt 16 connections at S146 (Apocalypse
-- of Abraham 13''s Azazel-tempting-Avraham is thematically-adjacent to
-- the Get-thee-behind-me-Satan substance at vv.22-23 but the Matt 4
-- wilderness-temptation parallel within-canon carries the load-bearing
-- anchor more directly; Sonnini''s Acts of Paul is the post-resurrec-
-- tion lost-sheep-mission extension and does not bear on the Matt 16
-- confession-and-passion-prediction substance). Historical-witness
-- editions (Josephus, M.R. James''s apocryphal NT, Lightfoot''s Apos-
-- tolic Fathers) remain deferred from V1 cross-refs per the historical-
-- witness one-way rule. The lookup view retains the full S139 edition
-- set for forward compatibility.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `the-son-of-the-living-elohim-named-before-the-foundation-in-1-enoch-and-wisdom-of-solomon`  (sort 302)
--   2. `the-elect-one-on-the-throne-and-the-davidic-stewardship-keys-in-1-enoch`                    (sort 303)
--   3. `the-righteous-one-condemned-with-a-shameful-death-in-wisdom-of-solomon`                     (sort 304)
--   4. `the-gates-of-sheol-and-the-resurrection-substance-in-wisdom-of-solomon-and-1-enoch`         (sort 305)
--   5. `reward-according-to-works-the-post-harvest-sifting-in-sirach-and-2-esdras`                  (sort 306)
--
-- 23 new cross_references rows at tier_required=''extras'' (Library tier,
-- $4.99) + 5 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required=''complete_study''
-- (Companion tier, $9.99). The tier split honors the two-layer architec-
-- ture of the chapter-end card: Layer 1 (per-verse cross-refs) visible to
-- Library readers who have access to the extras-library editions the
-- refs point to; Layer 2 (framework thread callouts with summary_md +
-- member_notes) gated at Companion, since the threads ARE the framework''s
-- reading of how canon and library answer each other — the "hidden detail
-- expand" that is the Companion-tier upgrade. Every member-note passes
-- the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial checklist; the seed-
-- mechanism per framework-deep''s *Paternal Seed and the Marriage-Coven-
-- ant Absorption* section + Red Line #7 augmentation does not surface in
-- Matt 16 (no foreign-origin individuals or seed-distinction substance
-- in the chapter — the chapter is internal to the inner-circle of the
-- disciples). Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el,
-- Ya''aqov, Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Sha''ul, Mikha''el, Gavri''el, Shemu''el,
-- Mosheh''s, King''s, Father''s, Yahuah''s, Yochanan''s, Kefa''s, etc.)
-- and English possessives (wisdom-stream''s, master''s, Father''s,
-- King''s, system''s, Pharisaic-system''s, Sadducean-system''s, etc.)
-- are escaped per SQL single-quoted-string-literal convention (every
-- internal ' doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 146 — Matt 16 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S145 view; retained for forward
-- compatibility even though Matt 16 does not surface Jubilees, Jasher,
-- Adam-Eve, Apocalypse-of-Abraham, Ascension-of-Isaiah, or Sonnini
-- Acts 29 connections at S146.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s146_verse_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 23 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1: the-son-of-the-living-elohim-named-before-the-foundation-in-1-enoch-and-wisdom-of-solomon
  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 13, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 46, 2,
   '*And I asked the angel who went with me, who showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, and why he went with the Head of Days.* 1 Enoch 46:2 names THE wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the *Son of Adam* title the King uses of himself at Matt 16:13 (*whom do men say that I the Son of Adam am?*). The Parables-of-Enoch (1 Enoch 37-71) had carried the Son-of-Adam title as a heavenly-figure-named-beside-the-Head-of-Days centuries before the King''s-incarnation; the King takes-up-the-title at the credentialing-question at Caesarea Philippi in continuity with the wisdom-stream''s articulation. The framework reads the substance carefully: the Son-of-Adam title carries the lineage-weight of the seed-of-Adam-line-of-promise per Red Line #12 the gospels restore from the translators''-flattening; 1 Enoch had named the title for the heavenly Christ at the Father''s right hand; the King names-himself by the same title at the gospel-pivot. The wisdom-stream and the gospel-substance cohere at the seed-of-Adam-line-of-promise architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 16, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 46, 3,
   '*This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, with whom dwelleth righteousness, and who reveals all the treasures of that which is hidden, because Yahuah (the Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, and whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (the Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* 1 Enoch 46:3 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Son-of-Adam''s identity at the depth the King carries at Matt 16:16. Kefa''s (Peter''s)-confession — *thou art the Messiah, the Son of the living Elohim (God)* — articulates at the gospel-pivot what the Parables-of-Enoch had named at the wisdom-stream-level: the Son-of-Adam is the Chosen-One in-whom-righteousness-dwells, the one-with-pre-eminence-before-Yahuah-of-Spirits. The framework reads the cause-and-effect-of-hearing per Red Line #11 operating across the gospel-pivot: Kefa (Peter) confesses because the Father has-revealed-the-substance (Matt 16:17''s *flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven*); the substance the Father reveals is the substance the wisdom-stream had named in the Parables-of-Enoch centuries before; the wisdom-stream and the gospel-confession cohere at the Son-of-Adam-as-the-Chosen-One-of-Yahuah-of-Spirits architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 16, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 48, 2,
   '*And at that hour that Son of Adam was named in the presence of Yahuah (God) of Spirits, and his name before the Head of Days.* 1 Enoch 48:2 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Son-of-Adam-being-named-in-the-presence-of-Yahuah-of-Spirits substance — the heavenly-naming-of-the-Christ at the throne. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:16''s *thou art the Messiah, the Son of the living Elohim (God).* Kefa''s (Peter''s)-confession articulates at the earthly-gospel-pivot what 1 Enoch 48:2 names at the heavenly-throne-pivot: the Son-of-Adam''s name is the name-named-before-the-Head-of-Days. The wisdom-stream had named the heavenly-substance; the gospel-confession lands the earthly-confession of the same architecture; the cause-and-effect-of-hearing per Red Line #11 operates at the Father''s-revealing the same substance the wisdom-stream carried.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 17, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 48, 3,
   '*Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made, his name was named before Yahuah (God) of Spirits.* 1 Enoch 48:3 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the before-the-foundation-of-the-world naming substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:17''s *flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven.* The Father''s-revelation to Kefa (Peter) reveals what was always true — the Son-of-Adam''s name was named-before-the-sun-and-the-signs-were-created, before-the-stars-of-the-heaven-were-made; the gospel-confession at Caesarea Philippi reveals at the earthly-historical-pivot the substance the wisdom-stream had named at the before-creation register. The framework reads this in continuity with Revelation 13:8 / 17:8''s *the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world* and *names written in the book of life from the foundation of the world* — the Father''s-foreknowledge architecture the cause-and-effect-of-hearing per Red Line #11 operates within.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 16, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 18,
   '*For if the just man be the son of Yahuah (God), he will help him, and deliver him from the hand of his enemies.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:18 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the just-man-as-the-son-of-Yahuah substance — the wicked''s-mocking-challenge against the righteous-one in the prefiguring-passage Wisdom of Solomon 2:12-20 carries. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:16''s *thou art the Messiah, the Son of the living Elohim (God).* Kefa''s (Peter''s)-confession articulates at the gospel-pivot the title the wisdom-stream had named in the prefiguring-of-the-righteous-one architecture: the just-man-is-the-son-of-Yahuah; the framework reads the substance against the inherited-Christian-Trinity-doctrine''s collapse and against the Trinity-denial''s collapse — the Son-of-Yahuah substance is the Formed-Voice''s relation-to-the-Formless-Source per the framework''s nature-of-God reading; the wisdom-stream had named the architecture in the prefiguring-passage; Kefa''s (Peter''s)-confession lands the operative-substance.'),

  -- Thread 2: the-elect-one-on-the-throne-and-the-davidic-stewardship-keys-in-1-enoch
  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 19, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 49, 2,
   '*For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, and unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow, and have no continuance; because the Elect One stands before Yahuah (the Lord) of Spirits.* 1 Enoch 49:2 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Elect-One-as-the-Standing-One-before-Yahuah-of-Spirits substance — the Christ-figure to-whom-the-secrets-of-righteousness-are-committed. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:19''s keys-of-the-kingdom delegated to the apostolic-stewardship. The Elect-One holds-the-secrets-of-righteousness at the wisdom-stream''s articulation; the King-as-the-Elect-One delegates the keys-of-the-kingdom-of-heaven (the binding-and-loosing-substance of vv.19) to the apostolic-stewardship at the gospel-pivot. The delegated-stewardship operates downstream-of-the-Elect-One''s-own-position-before-the-Father; the wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the Christ-as-the-Holder-of-the-Secrets; the King''s-delegation at Matt 16:19 operates within the Elect-One''s-own-master-authority.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 19, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 51, 3,
   '*And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, and his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: for Yahuah (the Lord) of Spirits hath given them to him and hath glorified him.* 1 Enoch 51:3 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the Elect-One-on-the-throne substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:19''s keys-of-the-kingdom-of-heaven committed to the apostolic-stewardship and against the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 22:22 *I will lay the key of the house of David upon his shoulder* the short.md walks at the Shevna-and-Elyakim succession depth. The Elect-One sits on Yahuah-of-Spirits''-throne; the keys-of-the-house-of-David belong to the Elect-One; the King delegates the keys-of-the-kingdom-of-heaven to the apostolic-stewardship from the throne-position 1 Enoch 51:3 had named the wisdom-stream-substance for. The framework reads this as FRAMEWORK-MAJOR for the apostolic-stewardship''s derivation from the King''s-own-throne-position.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 19, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 7,
   '*This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, and righteousness abides over him, and the righteousness of the Elect One of Yahuah (God) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and elect.* 1 Enoch 62:7 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Son-of-Adam revealed-to-the-holy-and-elect substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:17-19''s sequence: the Father reveals the Son-of-Adam to Kefa (Peter) (the just-blessed disciple is one of the holy-and-elect to whom the revelation comes); the revelation is followed by the King''s-delegation of the keys to the apostolic-stewardship. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the revelation-of-the-Son-of-Adam-to-the-elect; the gospel-pivot at Caesarea Philippi enacts the architecture in the historical-disciples'' confession.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 19, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 69, 27,
   '*And he sat on the throne of his glory, and the sum of judgment was given unto the Son of Adam, and he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth.* 1 Enoch 69:27 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the sum-of-judgment-given-unto-the-Son-of-Adam substance — the binding-and-loosing-and-judgment-authority committed-unto-the-Christ-on-the-throne-of-his-glory. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:19''s binding-and-loosing-authority delegated to the apostolic-stewardship. The sum-of-judgment belongs to the Son-of-Adam at the wisdom-stream''s articulation; the apostolic-stewardship''s binding-and-loosing operates downstream-of-and-in-accountability-to the Son-of-Adam''s-own-sum-of-judgment. The framework reads the binding-and-loosing-substance in continuity with the Tanakh-rabbinic *asar* (bind) and *hattir* (loose) — the apostolic-authority to declare-the-Torah''s-substance against-the-Pharisaic-tradition''s-corruption operates downstream-of-the-King''s-own-sum-of-judgment, NOT as a magisterial-authority-to-define-doctrine-against-scripture.'),

  -- Thread 3: the-righteous-one-condemned-with-a-shameful-death-in-wisdom-of-solomon
  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 21, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 12,
   '*Therefore let us lie in wait for the righteous; because he is not for our turn, and he is clean contrary to our doings: he upbraideth us with our offending the law, and objecteth to our infamy the transgressings of our education.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:12 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the wicked''s-plot-against-the-righteous-one substance — the prefiguring-passage Wisdom of Solomon 2:12-20 carries the architecture of the righteous-one persecuted-by-the-wicked-who-cannot-bear-his-reproof. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:21''s *he must go unto Yerushalayim (Jerusalem), and suffer many things of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the persecution-of-the-righteous-one centuries before; the King''s-first-passion-prediction names the operative-form: the elders-and-chief-priests-and-scribes (the Pharisaic-and-Sadducean-second-Temple-aristocracy) are the wicked-Wisdom-of-Solomon-2-names-in-the-prefiguring-architecture; the King is the righteous-one Wisdom-of-Solomon-2-names; the suffering-and-killing the King names is the operative-fulfillment of the architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 21, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 16,
   '*We are esteemed of him as counterfeits: he abstaineth from our ways as from filthiness: he pronounceth the end of the just to be blessed, and maketh his boast that Yahuah (God) is his father.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:16 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the wicked''s-grievance-against-the-righteous-one substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:21''s first-passion-prediction. The Pharisaic-and-Sadducean-second-Temple-aristocracy (the elders-and-chief-priests-and-scribes of v.21) reads the King''s-very-existence as the indictment-of-their-counterfeit-credentialing the King''s-Matt-23-woes will articulate explicitly; the wisdom-stream had named the architecture in the prefiguring-passage. The substance the King names at v.21 — that he MUST suffer at the hands-of-the-elders-and-chief-priests-and-scribes — operates in the architecture Wisdom of Solomon 2 had prefigured at the wisdom-stream-level centuries before.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 21, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 20,
   '*Let us condemn him with a shameful death: for by his own saying he shall be respected.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:20 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the wicked''s-condemnation-of-the-righteous-one-with-a-shameful-death substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:21''s *he must ... suffer many things ... and be killed.* The shameful-death the wisdom-stream had named is the cross-death the King will name explicitly at Matt 20:19 (*shall deliver him to the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify him*) and which the Devarim (Deuteronomy) 21:23 *cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree* substance Galatians 3:13 articulates at the apostolic-stream-level. The wisdom-stream-prefiguring at Wisdom of Solomon 2:20 + the Tanakh-suffering-servant of Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 53 + the gospel-passion-prediction at Matt 16:21 + the Devarim (Deuteronomy) 21:23 + Galatians 3:13 substance cohere at the shameful-death architecture the framework reads as the Father''s-Tanakh-bearing-substance the King is the operative-fulfillment of.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 21, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 3, 1,
   '*But the souls of the righteous are in the hand of Yahuah (God), and there shall no torment touch them.* Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the souls-of-the-righteous-preserved-in-the-Father''s-hand substance — the post-shameful-death vindication-architecture Wisdom of Solomon 3 unfolds (against the wicked''s-mocking-of-the-righteous-one in chapter 2). The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:21''s *and be raised again the third day.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the righteous-one''s-vindication after the shameful-death; the King''s-passion-prediction names both halves explicitly — the suffering-and-killing AND the third-day-raising. The resurrection-credential the sign-of-Yonah pre-announces at v.4 is the operative-fulfillment of the wisdom-stream-prefiguring at Wisdom of Solomon 3:1.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 21, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 5, 1,
   '*Then shall the righteous man stand in great boldness before the face of such as have afflicted him, and made no account of his labours.* Wisdom of Solomon 5:1 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the righteous-man''s-vindication-before-the-face-of-the-wicked substance — the post-resurrection-vindication-scene Wisdom of Solomon 5 unfolds. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:21''s *and be raised again the third day* and the broader-second-coming-vindication substance the *some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the Son of Adam coming in his kingdom* at v.28 carries-forward. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the vindication-of-the-righteous-one-before-the-face-of-his-afflicters; the King''s-first-passion-prediction at v.21 names the third-day-raising as the immediate-credential; the second-coming-substance at v.27 names the broader-vindication the wisdom-stream had named the architecture for. The framework reads the substance in continuity with the cause-and-effect-of-hearing of Red Line #11 — the righteous-one''s-vindication is the public-confirmation of what-was-always-true.'),

  -- Thread 4: the-gates-of-sheol-and-the-resurrection-substance-in-wisdom-of-solomon-and-1-enoch
  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 18, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 1, 13,
   '*For Yahuah (God) made not death: neither has he pleasure in the destruction of the living.* Wisdom of Solomon 1:13 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the death-is-not-from-Yahuah substance — the Father is not-the-source of the death-and-the-grave; the death-and-the-grave entered through the seed-war and the curse the Bereshit (Genesis) 3 narrative names. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:18''s *the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.* The gates-of-Sheol/Hades carry the power-of-death-and-the-grave that entered through the curse; the gates do not originate-with-the-Father; therefore the gates do not have permanence-against the assembly the King builds; therefore the resurrection-substance the King will demonstrate at the sign-of-Yonah breaks the gates'' hold. The wisdom-stream had named the death-is-not-from-Yahuah substance; the King''s-resurrection enacts the operative-substance.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 18, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 16, 13,
   '*For you have power of life and death: you leadest to the gates of hell, and bringest up again.* Wisdom of Solomon 16:13 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the gates-of-hell-and-the-bringing-up-again substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:18''s *the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: the Father has-power-of-life-and-death; the Father leads-to-the-gates-of-hell-and-brings-up-again; the gates-of-Sheol/Hades do not have-final-authority-against-the-Father''s-power-to-bring-up-again. The King''s-promise that the gates-of-hell shall not prevail against the assembly enacts the wisdom-stream-substance at the gospel-pivot: the assembly built on the resurrected-King partakes-of-the-bringing-up-again the Father''s-power has-always-held. The framework reads the substance in continuity with the resurrection-credential of the sign-of-Yonah pre-announced at v.4 and the explicit-third-day-raising at v.21.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 18, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 51, 1,
   '*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, and Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, and hell shall give back that which it owes.* 1 Enoch 51:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Sheol-giving-back-the-dead substance — the resurrection-architecture Wisdom of Solomon 16:13''s *bringest up again* substance names at the apocryphal-stream-level and 1 Enoch 51:1 articulates at the pseudepigraphal-stream-level. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:18''s *the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.* The gates-of-Sheol do not hold-finally because Sheol shall give-back-that-which-it-has-received at the day-of-Yahuah; the assembly built-on-the-King partakes-of-the-resurrection-substance the wisdom-stream had named the architecture for. The framework reads this in continuity with the broader-resurrection-architecture per the first-resurrection of Revelation 20:4-6 and the gathering-of-the-elect from-the-four-winds at Matt 24:31.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 18, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 4, 35,
   '*Did not the souls also of the righteous ask question of these things in their chambers, saying, How long shall I hope on this fashion? when comes the fruit of the floor of our reward?* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 4:35 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the souls-of-the-righteous-in-their-chambers substance — the waiting-room of the righteous-dead between the first-coming and the resurrection. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:18''s gates-of-hell-shall-not-prevail substance. The chambers-of-the-righteous-souls are not the eternal-conscious-torment-hell of the inherited-Christian-doctrine; the chambers are the waiting-place-for-the-resurrection. The gates-of-Sheol the King names do not hold-the-righteous-souls-finally; the resurrection-architecture per Red Line #11''s sequence the framework reads operates: the righteous-souls in-the-chambers await-the-first-resurrection at the King''s-coming, when Sheol gives back-that-which-it-has-received (1 Enoch 51:1) and the chambers-deliver-those-souls-that-were-committed-unto-them (2 Esdras 7:32''s parallel naming).'),

  -- Thread 5: reward-according-to-works-the-post-harvest-sifting-in-sirach-and-2-esdras
  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 27, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 16, 12,
   '*As his mercy is great, so is his correction also: he judges a man according to his works.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16:12 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Father-judges-a-man-according-to-his-works substance — both the mercy and the correction operating from the Father''s-righteous-character. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:27''s *the Son of Adam shall come in the glory of his Father with his angels; and then he shall reward every man according to his works.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the judgment-according-to-works; the King''s-second-coming-substance operates the same architecture at the eschatological-consummation. The framework reads this in continuity with the post-harvest-sifting per Red Line #11 — the works are the fruit-of-the-new-heart-that-internalized-or-did-not-internalize per the Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27 substance; the wisdom-stream had named the architecture; the King names the operative-form at the gospel-precision.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 27, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 16, 14,
   '*Make way for every work of mercy: for every man shall find according to his works.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16:14 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the every-man-shall-find-according-to-his-works substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:27''s reward-according-to-works at the Son-of-Adam''s-coming. The wisdom-stream had named the universal-substance: every-man finds-according-to-his-works at the day-of-judgment. The King''s-articulation at v.27 names the operative-form at the second-coming. The framework reads this in continuity with the framework''s-grace-and-the-opportunity-that-can-be-lost architecture — the grace is the door-home; the works are the fruit; the reward at the day-of-judgment operates according-to-the-fruit, in the post-harvest-sifting Matt 7:21-23 + Matt 13:36-43 + Matt 25:31-46 articulate at the gospel-substance the wisdom-stream had named.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 27, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 35, 19,
   '*Till he have rendered to every man according to his deeds, and to the works of men according to their devices; till he have judged the cause of his people, and made them to rejoice in his mercy.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 35:19 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the rendering-to-every-man-according-to-his-deeds substance — paired with the judging-of-the-cause-of-the-Father''s-people substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:27''s reward-according-to-works at the Son-of-Adam''s-coming. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the rendering-according-to-deeds AND the judging-of-the-cause-of-the-Father''s-people in the same breath — both halves of the day-of-judgment substance. The King''s-articulation at v.27 carries-forward both halves: the reward-according-to-works for the sifted-wheat AND the judging-of-the-cause-of-the-Father''s-people in the millennial-reign-on-the-earth. The framework reads this in continuity with the Tehillim (Psalm) 62:12 *thou renderest to every man according to his work* substance Romans 2:6 cites at the apostolic-level.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 27, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 32,
   '*And the earth shall restore those that are asleep in her, and so shall the dust those that dwell in silence, and the secret places shall deliver those souls that were committed unto them.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:32 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the resurrection-of-the-dead substance preceding the day-of-judgment. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:27''s Son-of-Adam-coming-and-rewarding substance. The resurrection-substance the wisdom-stream names at 2 Esdras 7:32 + 1 Enoch 51:1 + Wisdom of Solomon 16:13 precedes the rewarding-according-to-works at the day-of-judgment. The framework reads the sequence in continuity with the first-resurrection of Revelation 20:4-6 — the righteous-souls in-the-chambers (2 Esdras 4:35) are restored-and-delivered (2 Esdras 7:32) and the works-of-the-living-and-the-restored are sifted-and-rewarded (2 Esdras 7:35 + Sirach 16:12 + Matt 16:27).'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 16, 27, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 35,
   '*And the work shall follow, and the reward shall be shewed, and the good deeds shall be of force, and wicked deeds shall bear no rule.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:35 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the work-shall-follow-and-the-reward-shall-be-shewed substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 16:27''s *he shall reward every man according to his works.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture: the work follows the man into the day-of-judgment; the reward is shown according to the work; the good deeds operate at the day; the wicked deeds bear no rule. The King''s-articulation at v.27 names the operative-form at the Son-of-Adam''s-coming. The framework reads the substance in continuity with the post-harvest-sifting per Red Line #11 and with the cause-and-effect-of-hearing — the works-that-follow are the fruit-of-the-new-heart-that-internalized; the works-that-do-not-follow surface the unfruitful-wheat per the Matt 7:23 *I never knew you, depart from me, ye that work iniquity* substance.')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s146_verse_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug = i.src_edition
                            AND sv.book_slug    = i.src_slug
                            AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                            AND sv.verse_number  = i.src_v
  JOIN _s146_verse_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug = i.tgt_edition
                            AND tv.book_slug    = i.tgt_slug
                            AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                            AND tv.verse_number  = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

